      "source_section": "Statement and Proof steps 1.1–2.1",
      "quote": "The Statement gives the bounded-square product error. Proof 1.1 defines $P_{M,\\varepsilon}(x,y)=2M^2[Q_\\delta(|x+y|/(2M))-Q_\\delta(|x|/(2M))-Q_\\delta(|y|/(2M))]$. Proof 2.1 states that $Q_\\delta(0)=0$ makes the formula cancel on either coordinate axis; since the displayed ReLU formula is globally defined, the cancellation holds for every real value of the other input.",
